      "content": "Running coding agents safely in production requires solving a hard infrastructure problem: isolated execution environments. When an agent executes shell commands and edits code, you cannot let it run unchecked inside your primary services or rely on brittle local runners.\n\nCodex Session Operator manages this by provisioning isolated Kubernetes sandboxes for OpenAI Managed Agents. While OpenAI handles the inference and agentic loop, the operator isolates arbitrary command execution and Git workspace persistence inside Kubernetes Agent Sandboxes, persisting session transcripts and approval states back to PostgreSQL.\n\nDecoupling the agent reasoning loop from the containerized execution boundary is the right operational pattern for production-grade agent platforms."
    },
    {
      "title": "Virtual scrolling and cached watches accelerate large cluster inspection",
